# The Vanishing Point

`perspective` is a parent property that defines the distance between the viewer and the screen. Smaller values = more dramatic perspective.

```css
.scene {
  perspective: 600px;
}
.box {
  transform: rotateY(30deg);
}
```
Without perspective on the parent, `rotateY()` looks flat. You can also use `perspective()` function inside the transform but the parent approach is more realistic.

